00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
well let's head back to that breaking  news now the historic deal brokered by  the u.s to normalize relations between  the uae and israel harry fawcett is live  for us now  in west jerusalem harry how major a  development is this  uh it's a huge development this is  something that benjamin netanyahu has  been  talking about and working towards for  much of his political career the idea of  normalizing relations  between israel and its important uh  arab muslim neighbors in the region and  this is the first such  agreement in full he has been working uh  on various  levels uh trying to to get better ties  and has  celebrated various minor victories in  terms of minor improvements  with various neighbors but this  according to the joint statement  released by the united states by israel  and by the uae  amounts to a full normalization and a  development of  full ties between the two countries the  statement says that  the delegations from both countries will  meet in the coming weeks  to sign these agreements that there will  be uh normalization of diplomatic ties  of  economic medical technological  telecommunications cooperation  direct flights between israel and the  uae tourist flights  as well as business flights and  importantly it also says that as a  result  of what this statement calls a historic  breakthrough  uh israel will suspend its efforts to  annex parts of the occupied west bank  the parts  of the west bank that were designated to  be israeli territory  under the trump jared kushner peace plan  which had created such a great deal of  heat and noise  in recent months with benjamin  netanyahu's vow to just move ahead  with u.s support and start annexing well  ahead of any  potential agreement with the  palestinians now that is  suspended in its entirety and instead  the statement says israel will work on  expanding its relations with other  muslim arab countries in the region um  i haven't seen any reaction yet from the  palestinian side from  allah but i think the reaction would be  that israel appears to be being rewarded  for not doing something  rather than having any real progress in  terms of the  the peace process between uh israel and  the palestinians  of course under the arab peace  initiative there should come  first a settlement to the  israeli-palestinian conflict before  any normalization so this is uh is a  major upset in terms of  what had been the uh the sort of  explicit thinking and policy  of arab states up until this point think  of that we'll leave it there for now  uh harry fawcett live for us from west  jerusalem alan fisher  joins us now live uh from washington d.c  for u.s  reaction alan i mean this was brokered  by the us this is going to be seen as a  huge win for donald trump  well certainly it came from donald trump  just in the oval office not far from  where i'm standing just a few minutes  ago he was surrounded  by his senior advisers we'll get the  tape of that announcement  very shortly probably within the next  few minutes he said that the  announcement had been made that the  united arab emirates and israel were  normalizing relations that they were  going to sign  some sort of treaty and that other arab  countries  would follow he said there are things  happening that he couldn't talk about  at this point now clearly this is  something that  will please the trump administration it  is a big  foreign policy win as harry was saying  there has been  the kushner peace plan for the middle  east which has stalled going absolutely  nowhere  that was revealed several months ago and  has absolutely  done nothing since that point and so  there'll be questions though  about why the united arab emirates and  israel if there was something as  significant  and as fundamental as a peace deal to be  announced between  these two countries why the leaders  themselves  wouldn't announce it why they would  allow donald trump to do that from the  oval office  is this perhaps a sign that both  countries would like to aid donald  trump's re-election effort  in some way we know that israel are very  close  is very close to donald trump they  believe that he has been a huge  supporter  during his time in the oval office from  moving  the embassy to jerusalem to recognizing  israeli sovereignty over the occupied  golan heights  there was some concern too that the  white house would give the go-ahead to  allow  israel to annex parts of the west bank  although that  was stopped it ran into the mud over the  last few weeks or so  and we know that the united arab  emirates enjoy a good relationship  uh with donald trump as does saudi  arabia and so  there will be political questions about  this but certainly as far as donald  trump and the white house is concerned  this is a major diplomatic victory and  uh alan as you sort of mentioned there  the u.s  had recently sort of taken the foot off  the gas in terms of their support  for those annexation plans hadn't they  had this been sort of  uh you know were there signs that this  might be on the way  well there was no indication in fact i i  got a phone call  probably about five ten minutes before  the announcement was made to tell me  there was a big announcement coming and  it involved israel and the united arab  emirates  i then started making several calls  myself to try and establish it  and then we heard that donald trump was  making the announcement  in the oval office himself uh  it's an interesting state of affairs  because we know that donald trump tried  to get a peace deal with north korea  that's essentially lying in tatters at  the moment we know that they've  exercised  the the campaign of maximum pressure on  iran to try and bring them  to the negotiating table that had failed  and we saw the failure of that  personified in the fact  that brian hooke who is the main  negotiator the point man on  all talks with iran left his post  just the other week and we know that  kellyanne conway stood on the driveway  that you see behind me  in the white house saying that she  expected an announcement from the  president  about annexation and we thought that  that meant he was going to give the okay  for that and that was several weeks ago  and then nothing happened there were  technical points to be discussed  so whether or not the whole discussion  between israel and the united arab  emirates  gained momentum at that point i think  will become clear when people start to  write their books about this moment in  history  but clearly the the trump white house  was looking  for a foreign policy victory because  they've had precious few  of them up to this point and so to be  able to sit down  in the oval office and as the president  of the united states announced  that there was going to be a peace deal  between the uae and  israel unusual though that is it  certainly signifies a big win for donald  trump and something that he needed given  that  the past 48 hours has been dominated by  joe biden and his pick for vice  president  thank you so much for that ellen fischer  there live in washington d.c

